From e5174b480abcee605ccebf770f265e2b0181d359 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nekokabu <nekokabu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:28:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 31/32] n64: the VI loads the bus only while it reads the
 picture (task_timing v26)

The VI factors of the timing model (how much longer the RDP's spans and
loads take, what a CPU or SP DMA transfer costs the RDP, how long an SP
DMA and a CPU cache line transfer take themselves) were measured as the
time of a whole list or task with the VI on over that with it off, and
applied at every moment. But the VI reads RDRAM only on the lines of the
picture (VI_V_VIDEO): for 0.097 VI of every field, the vertical
blanking, it leaves the bus alone.

Console (task_timing v26, Beetle Adventure Racing (J) intro tasks
replayed, the RDP's progress sampled every 1/50 VI): relative to the
same task with the VI off the RDP runs at 0.85 to 0.91 of its speed
before and after the blanking and at 0.96 to 1.01 during it.

The replays start at a known line (VI_V_CURRENT 330 of 525, 1 ms before
the task) and spend 12 to 17% of their time in the blanking. The game
starts its graphics task 0.08 VI after the VI interrupt, just as the
picture begins, so a task shorter than 0.89 VI never sees a blanking.
Frame by frame against the game's own log (bar_tasklog with the CPU
waiting, the content of a frame is fixed by its number) the same task
took 0.025 to 0.041 VI longer in the game than replayed; the model had
0.003 to 0.005. This was most of what the first scene's light frames
lacked (go to RSP done -4.8% in frames 20 to 39 with the CPU waiting;
the CPU's part, normal minus waiting, was within 0.87 to 1.13 of the
console's).

- VI::picture(): the VI is on a line of the picture.
- Spans and loads are priced as if the VI read the picture all the
  time; the part the VI adds is kept apart (timing.pendingVi) and not
  spent while the VI is outside the picture (timingStep).
- The transfer losses (contendScale), the megabyte-of-the-VI terms of
  CPU transfers and SP DMAs, the SP DMA's own duration and the CPU's VI
  stall apply only inside the picture.
- Inside the picture every VI part is 1.16 times what it was
  (timing.viPicture): with that the six replays of task_timing v26 keep
  their measured time (model minus console +0.10% on average, as before).

Results (console): Beetle Adventure Racing intro, first scene 232
frames (231; was 239), every block of 60 VI within one frame; second
scene 319 (325; was 323). Donkey Kong 64 DKTV demo frame deltas 2 / 3 /
4+ = 11 / 378 / 33 (9 / 388 / 25; was 10 / 376 / 34). MGC 2011 demo
unchanged (parts within -0.1 to +0.2%, part 5 +1.3%, "@" +20 VI).
